# Local CI before commit

## Scoped gate (every task commit and verifier Layer 2)

Map staged/committed paths → package filter(s). Run **only** affected packages — not the full monorepo unless the task touched root tooling.

```bash
bash scripts/with-ci-env.sh pnpm turbo run lint typecheck test:unit --filter=...
```

Examples by stack (customize in project-setup):

```bash
# pnpm + turbo monorepo (Escalite default)
bash scripts/with-ci-env.sh pnpm turbo run lint typecheck test:unit --filter=@escalite/web

# Go API only (full monorepo Go gate)
bash scripts/go-test.sh

# Go API only (scoped package)
cd services/api && go test ./...
```

Mark checks `n/a` when not defined for the current phase (e.g. pre-Phase 0 docs-only work). On failure → `blocked`; no commit.

## Full gate (pre-push only)

When the user **explicitly asks to push**:

```bash
bash scripts/with-ci-env.sh pnpm turbo run lint typecheck test:unit
```

Sub-agents must **not** run the full gate during routine task execution unless push is requested.

## Rules

- Derive `--filter` from WRITE ∪ READ scope paths (see `doc-index.md` or `02-orchestrator.mdc`).
- Docs-only / `.cursor/**` changes: skip monorepo gate; run targeted validation only.
- Lane P parallel agents: use per-worktree `WORK_ROOT`; never global `pkill` that kills sibling agents.
